    "result_text": "The build passes. Only one test class exists in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`):\n\n- Added a static SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n  ```java\n  private static final Logger auditLogger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n  ```\n- Emitted the audit line immediately after the successful `saveOwner(...)` call, once the owner's `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` are all populated:\n  ```java\n  auditLogger.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nPlacing the log after `saveOwner` is important: the id is assigned by persistence, `customerCode` is generated inside `saveOwner`, and `registrationDate` is resolved earlier in the method \u2014 so the logged values exactly match what `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns, which is what `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` asserts via the `AUDIT` logger capture.\n\nThe full test suite runs green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
