        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is minimal, additive, and idiomatic. The audit logger is a `private static final` SLF4J `Logger` obtained via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` \u2014 the conventional way to get a named (non-class) logger \u2014 and the single `auditLogger.info(...)` call sits immediately after `saveOwner(...)`, exactly at the \"successful create\" point, with the three required fields passed as parameterized arguments. It lives in the `addOwner` endpoint, which is the natural unit for \"on successful create,\" and there's no existing audit/logging infrastructure elsewhere to route through, so a service-layer hook would be over-engineering for this scope. No duplication, no bloat, nothing turning into a catch-all. A maintainer of this Spring codebase would read it as ordinary."
